Sogen: ReadFile and WriteFile on a non-blocking socket pend

afd.sys serves a socket's IRP_MJ_READ and IRP_MJ_WRITE as overlapped
requests, which pend until the socket is ready whatever its blocking
mode. Sogen answered them as it answers a receive or a send on a
non-blocking socket: STATUS_DEVICE_NOT_READY at once.

WSAEventSelect makes a socket non-blocking, and accept gives the socket
it returns the listener's mode. usocket waits for hunchentoot's
connections that way, so each worker's socket was non-blocking; SBCL
reads and writes sockets with ReadFile and WriteFile, and took the
worker's first read before the client had written as an I/O error. The
worker closed the connection: warm.lisp's WebSocket attach lost its
socket after the handshake, and the build stopped at "the sync stream
never replayed".

ReadFile and WriteFile on a socket now pend on either mode; the
receive and send requests keep their answer for a non-blocking socket.

